WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.000
Break open a maize kernel.

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.040
Part of it is a baby plant, part is its food, and part is a wrapper.

3
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.740
Which parts came from the father?

4
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.353
We can answer by counting chromosome sets.

5
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:20.853
One set is the chromosomes of one egg or one sperm.

6
00:00:22.073 --> 00:00:24.113
The mother's sets will be magenta blocks.

7
00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:26.733
The father's will be teal.

8
00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:28.883
Start with the father.

9
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:31.763
A pollen grain is not a sperm.

10
00:00:33.063 --> 00:00:37.943
It is a tiny separate generation of the plant, two or three cells, and it makes two

11
00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:38.943
sperm.

12
00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:42.677
Every cell in the grain carries one set from the father.

13
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:47.357
The grain lands on a stigma, the sticky tip that catches pollen.

14
00:00:48.657 --> 00:00:52.497
It grows a tube down to an ovule, and the two sperm ride inside.

15
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:58.097
Inside the ovule waits the mother's tiny generation, the embryo sac.

16
00:00:59.337 --> 00:01:03.937
It comes from one spore, so its nuclei are all copies of one maternal set.

17
00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:06.587
Three kinds of cells matter.

18
00:01:07.927 --> 00:01:09.627
The egg holds one magenta block.

19
00:01:10.887 --> 00:01:15.047
The large central cell holds two identical copies of that same set.

20
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.087
Two synergids sit beside the egg.

21
00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:21.067
The synergids signal to the tube.

22
00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:25.487
The tube bursts into one of them and releases both sperm.

23
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.580
One sperm fuses with the egg.

24
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.400
That makes the zygote, which grows into the embryo.

25
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.580
Its stack is one magenta block and one teal.

26
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.290
The other sperm fuses with the central cell.

27
00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.270
That cell already holds two copies of the mother's set.

28
00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.410
How many blocks will the new tissue carry?

29
00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.030
How many are the father's?

30
00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:58.563
Three blocks, only one of them teal.

31
00:01:59.643 --> 00:02:04.703
This is the endosperm, the food store for the embryo: two maternal sets, one

32
00:02:04.703 --> 00:02:05.703
paternal.

33
00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:09.977
One sperm starts the baby plant, and the other starts its food.

34
00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:12.797
This is double fertilization.

35
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:17.610
Layers of the mother's own tissue surround the embryo sac.

36
00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.470
They become the seed coat, with no teal at all.

37
00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:25.930
The ovary wall around the ovule becomes the fruit wall.

38
00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.670
It is the mother's tissue too.

39
00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.270
In maize, it is the kernel's thin outer skin.

40
00:02:33.333 --> 00:02:35.253
One kernel, three ledgers.

41
00:02:36.513 --> 00:02:37.553
Embryo, one and one.

42
00:02:38.633 --> 00:02:40.453
Endosperm, two and one.

43
00:02:41.693 --> 00:02:43.313
Coat and fruit wall, two and none.

44
00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:46.787
This count holds for most flowering plants.

45
00:02:48.147 --> 00:02:51.207
Water lilies, for one, change the numbers but keep the logic.

46
00:02:52.317 --> 00:02:54.937
Pollen landing on a stigma is pollination.

47
00:02:56.397 --> 00:03:00.797
Fertilization comes later, inside the ovule, and only if a tube arrives.

48
00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.930
So the father sends one set, twice.

49
00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.270
His sets enter only the embryo and the endosperm.

50
00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.410
The seed coat and fruit wall are the mother's own tissue.
